My father is a Half-Orc
And my mother is an Elf. 
I'm a credit to my family
And I'm in the best of health.

Yes my Mummy is a Wood Elf,
And my Daddy's half an Orc
While his other half is human
(Though the neighbours love to talk).

From Father I have gained my strength,
My stamina, my speed.
(So if I have to fight someone
I can kill him if I need.) 

From Mother I've inherited 
My intellegence and grace.
And I thank my lucky stars
That I've inherited her face

All in all I'm pretty lucky -
Yes, I have to say I'm glad
That my muscles aren't my mother's
And my looks don't come from Dad


Todays Moral: There's nothing Moral about the union of an Elf and a Half-Orc.
